WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.312 --> 00:00:02.420
- How does southeastern Wisconsin fit

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:05.070
into this national election picture?

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.110
- I mean it's battle ground zero, right?

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:10.040
We've always been a battleground but,

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:11.440
always at the end of these elections,

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:12.500
it seems to have faded away

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:15.060
and other States have become more focused.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.900
I think Wisconsin is a great place

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.770
and I think that even
when we have differences,

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.600
we can a have a beer and a brat, right?

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.410
- [Narrator] Roughly half
of America's voters live

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:24.340
in the suburbs,

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:26.140
and in the final months of the campaign,

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.270
as president Trump seeks
to boost his support

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:29.260
in those communities,

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:32.240
he has zeroed in on the
threat of violent crime.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.040
- The suburbs are coming big to us

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.380
because the suburbs are next.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.170
If you elected this guy,

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:42.957
the suburbs would be overwhelmed
with violence and crime.

00:00:42.957 --> 00:00:45.480
[Narrator] And Wisconsin, a swing state,

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.280
is likely to be some of the
most fought over ground.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.070
In 2016, President Trump won here by fewer

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.270
than 23,000 votes.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:54.620
- [News Anchor] He will win Wisconsin,

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.430
with its 10 electoral votes

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:58.790
he's cracked the so called, "Blue wall"

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:00.240
- [Narrator] A Marquette Law School poll

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.720
of likely Wisconsin voters

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:04.840
from early September showed
former vice president Joe Biden

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:08.860
leading president Trump 47% to 43%.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:11.130
Three suburban counties
around Milwaukee serve

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.550
as a GOP counterweight

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:15.260
to the traditionally large
democratic margins recorded

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:19.240
in the State's two largest
cities, Milwaukee and Madison.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.100
The president will likely need to win big

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.200
in the suburban counties

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.340
if he wants to take the state again.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:25.940
We sat down with a group of voters

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.330
from Waukesha and Ozaukee counties,

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:32.330
half voted for Trump and half
voted for Clinton in 2016,

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:36.120
to discuss the coronavirus
pandemic, the economy, policing

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.910
and how they are weighing a
sudden supreme court vacancy,

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.530
as they think about November's election.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:44.340
- Did anybody really sort of struggle

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:46.397
with that decision in 2016?

00:01:46.397 --> 00:01:50.895
- I actually voted
Republican in 2008, in 2012

00:01:50.895 --> 00:01:55.895
and then in 2016, I voted
Democrat for the first time,

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:59.920
in my case was because of the
person instead of the party.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.850
I couldn't vote for Donald Trump.

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:05.350
- Raise your hands if you plan
to vote for president Trump

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:06.643
between now and November.

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:12.323
And who plans to vote for Joe Biden?

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.640
Sabrina it seemed like your hand raise

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.066
on Joe Biden was a little bit lukewarm.

00:02:20.066 --> 00:02:23.600
- Yes, I do want him to
show up more strongly

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:27.260
on some issues so I'm
still listening closely.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.650
- He might not get your vote?

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:31.653
- It's completely possible, yes.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:36.750
- On Memorial Day weekend
George Floyd was killed

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:40.180
in Minneapolis neighboring
state to Wisconsin,

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:43.053
and then subsequently in the summer,

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:48.060
another man was shot in Kenosha by police.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.520
I wanna get your sense for sort

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:53.070
of the Black Lives Matter movement,

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.253
there's been calls for police reform,

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:00.110
it's obviously a challenging topic

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.750
to talk about race in America,

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:03.820
but let's try to talk
about it a little bit

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.320
and see where you're feeling in terms

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:08.620
of how these protests have gone,

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:12.070
sometimes they've moved into riots

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:15.430
and what you think should be
done in terms of police reform.

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:17.710
- There's over 700,000 law enforcement

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.430
in the country right now

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:22.690
that we can expect those human
beings in those situations,

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:24.980
those conditions with that responsibility

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.450
to act flawlessly as ridiculous.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.740
And one is even more childish is to think

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:32.620
that we can improve that
by reducing the amount

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:33.960
of law enforcement.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:35.700
It's super unfortunate

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:40.660
that there are situations
like Floyd that do arise,

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:43.610
but when it comes to the numbers
itself and the interaction

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.160
and the people we're dealing
with, they are people,

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.930
yeah, there could be a little
bit more reform in terms

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.320
of making people
accountable for their jobs

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.060
in the proper way and
making sure they're not

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:58.160
on the force if they're not capable.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.920
- Sabrina, you've talked a little bit

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.550
about the segregation that
exists in this metropolitan area.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:04.746
What is your take?

00:04:04.746 --> 00:04:09.746
- It would be hypocritical
to be an American per se

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.520
and not understand that we have a history

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:13.788
of violence in this country.

00:04:13.788 --> 00:04:17.850
Unfortunately, change has
come through violence.

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:19.530
It's not the way that I want it to be.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.720
I'd love to come to the table

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:23.170
and talk it out and
just get rid of the ills

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:26.050
of our country but
that's not what happened.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:29.570
So understanding that racism
has seeped into so many parts

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:34.570
of our country, just it's as
American as apple pie, right?

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.210
There has to be reform within healthcare,

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.970
there has to be reformed within housing,

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:42.010
there has to be reformed within
the criminal justice system,

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.810
there has to be reformed in immigration.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:47.550
We have all these areas that
we have to dismantle racism

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:52.550
and become aware of our unconscious
bias and choose justice.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:53.573
- When they talk about,

00:04:53.573 --> 00:04:57.060
well only a few people have
been shot or killed or whatever,

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:58.390
that's just the tip of the iceberg.

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:00.580
It's really a lot more
than just a few bad apples.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:01.770
It's really systematic.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:05.370
I do feel that Trump
really incites the violence

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:08.390
and incites the divisiveness
and incites on the hate.

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:10.350
- The root of the problem
is systemic racism.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:12.570
We can't just turn a blind eye and say,

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:15.410
oh, you know, everything's fine.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:18.940
And it starts with
opportunities and the economy.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:21.700
Like you said we have a segregated city.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:25.150
Look at the resources we're
providing to the South side

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.370
and the North side of Milwaukee

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:31.160
versus a predominantly
white area like Brookfield

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:33.140
and Waukesha County,

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:35.510
the resources are day and night.

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:38.310
How do we expect people to be okay?

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:39.143
- Sue your turn.

00:05:39.143 --> 00:05:43.430
What's are your observations
about the summer of unrest

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:45.450
that took place in this country?

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:46.660
Well, I guess I don't understand

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.150
why people think it's Trump's fault

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:49.850
that all this is going on.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:53.050
I was always taught as
a young child growing up

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:57.940
that if a police officer tells
you to stop, you stopped.

00:05:57.940 --> 00:05:59.210
I don't care what color you are,

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.030
black, white, yellow, or purple.

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:04.270
These people deal with
people that are on drugs,

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:06.940
people that are crazy and
so I could see how some

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:08.670
of these police officers are nudge,

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:11.190
now we have some of them
taking it way too far?

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:12.333
Yes, they do believe so.

00:06:12.333 --> 00:06:14.990
And I'm not saying they were right

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:17.660
in what I think is torturing George Floyd.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:18.980
That certainly is not right

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.580
but there needs to be a little bit

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:26.580
of acceptance on both sides
that both sides did wrong.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:29.820
- Tamir Rice was shot
before he had any chance

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:32.020
to respond to any kind of police order.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:35.190
So the narrative that people
aren't following directions,

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:38.040
isn't completely true unfortunately

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.350
I've had police approached me

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:41.870
when their hands are
literally on their weapon

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:43.380
if they're coming up to me,

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.970
and my kids are right there seeing this.

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:48.620
So it's not that folks
are necessarily attempting

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:50.520
to not listen to police,

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:52.730
I think that narrative has to go.

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:54.410
- My father is a retired police officer.

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:57.530
So I have the utmost respect for police.

00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:59.260
And I think our big problem too is a lot

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:00.520
of the words we use,

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.100
the terminology, defund the
police, that's a bad term.

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:04.880
I wish nobody had put that term out there.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:06.220
It's not about taking away money

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:07.520
or taking away police officers.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:09.310
It's really, most of us want,

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:11.430
we want better education
for police officers,

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:12.870
we want more support for them,

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:15.650
social workers coming in
on some of these calls.

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:18.130
- Sabrina, can you just talk a little bit

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:20.180
about your vote and how you are feeling

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.771
about former vice president Joe Biden?

00:07:22.771 --> 00:07:26.929
- I do feel like Joe Biden
recently he started a campaign

00:07:26.929 --> 00:07:29.460
or at least his team started a campaign

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:32.650
of being more harsh on the variety.

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:34.347
When I think about Philando Castile

00:07:34.347 --> 00:07:36.680
and being murdered in Minnesota,

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.250
and then I think about what happened

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:40.810
with George Floyd being
murdered in Minnesota,

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:44.070
again same place, same kind of injustice

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:45.540
but there wasn't really change

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:47.817
or a movement until
George Floyd was murdered

00:07:47.817 --> 00:07:52.360
and the public had an
uprising, same state.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:57.360
So people don't listen until
things get out of hand per se.

00:07:57.550 --> 00:08:00.390
So I really don't like the
messaging of Joe Biden.

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:04.610
I do want him to stand with
the fact that there's injustice

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:05.940
that needs to be fixed.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:08.740
There are people being crushed
underneath these systems

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:11.060
and they are Americans also.

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:13.701
And when we say defund the
police, we definitely mean it.

00:08:13.701 --> 00:08:16.480
I don't wanna lose that message either,

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:18.810
we do mean defund the police
- We do

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:22.980
- Because we want systems that
actually do support people

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:26.440
in the ways that policing can not.

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:29.710
- We're sitting down just
days after the passing

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:33.820
of Ruth Bader Ginsburg leaving a seat open

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.110
on the Supreme court.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:38.010
How many of you think

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:40.530
that seat should be filled still

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:43.530
during Donald Trump's first term?

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:45.630
- Well, obviously we have a constitution,

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:48.660
it's by the advice and
consent of the Senate.

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:50.960
The Senate is Republican.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.150
If the president wants

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:54.310
to put forward his
nominee he has his right.

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:57.250
He's still the until January.

00:08:57.250 --> 00:08:59.320
- Well, I agree with
Chris, I'm gonna qualify it

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:00.153
though there's one thing

00:09:00.153 --> 00:09:03.020
that concerns me the most
is what implications will be

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:06.497
on the election if in
fact that president Trump

00:09:06.497 --> 00:09:09.200
and the Senate goes forward
with the nomination.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.070
I'd hate to think

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.930
that pushing this forward would

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:15.670
put president Trump's re-election at risk

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:18.730
or some of the senators
that are up for reelection.

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:19.563
- Sabrina talk a little bit

00:09:19.563 --> 00:09:23.430
about why you don't think it
should be filled this year.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:25.920
- Just looking at the
last example of the way

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:27.770
that Republicans stood up and said no,

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:31.370
Barack Obama cannot bring
somebody into this role

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:34.310
when he had more time than this one,

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:36.080
then I would say the same thing.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:38.170
- Lets pivot to a subject

00:09:38.170 --> 00:09:40.270
that really has dominated obviously all

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:44.270
of our lives practically all
year, and that's the pandemic.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:47.170
How many of you routinely
wear a mask when you go out

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:48.720
in public pretty much anywhere?

00:09:50.710 --> 00:09:51.830
- Well it depends.

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:53.810
I mean if some place where I
know there's gonna be a lot

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:56.350
of people that of course
I will wear a mask,

00:09:56.350 --> 00:10:00.150
but if I'm taking my dogs
for a walk by myself,

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:02.090
I'm not gonna put a mask on.

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:04.610
- Well, again, it goes back
to the inconsistent messaging

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:06.630
about the effectiveness of mask.

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:09.700
There is this like a
virtual signaling issue

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:12.790
with mask out there at this point as well.

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:14.247
It does come down to sort

00:10:14.247 --> 00:10:17.280
of what are our rights as citizens?

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:18.250
- The president has talked

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:23.250
about having a vaccine potentially
in time for the election.

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:24.950
What do you all think of about,

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:28.350
who do you believe when
it comes to the vaccine?

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:31.350
- So to try to get a vaccine
out and mask produced

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:33.520
and available in a matter of weeks

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:37.790
or months it's not
possible, it's not safe.

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:40.603
- Who all do you listen to
in terms of trusting what

00:10:40.603 --> 00:10:42.280
to know about the vaccine?

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.880
Who do you trust in terms of that topic?

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:47.020
- I think it was hard
when the CDC came out

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:48.400
or somebody came out and originally said,

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:50.370
mask don't help , don't use masks.

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:53.530
and that made it really hard
for a lot of people to trust.

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:54.970
But I think we didn't
know what we didn't know

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:57.770
and we shouldn't have assumed
that we knew something.

00:10:57.770 --> 00:11:00.390
I definitely I still
listen to file sheets,

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:02.523
I try to trust the CDC.

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:05.910
I think unfortunately they've
been influenced politically

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:06.980
when they shouldn't be,

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:10.090
but I think they're
still a reputable source.

00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:13.410
- Chris who do you trust in on this topic?

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:14.760
- Well, it's what's stunning

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:17.540
to me I think is doctors are
starting to sound like lawyers.

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:19.810
There's a lot of different
opinions and none of them seem

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:22.070
to agree which always worries me.

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:24.830
My nephew was just diagnosed with COVID,

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:27.550
asymptomatic no issues.

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:28.713
I have two assistants,

00:11:28.713 --> 00:11:30.840
one of my assistants got COVID.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:34.160
So it's affected me personally
but I'm not sure who

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:34.993
to believe on it

00:11:34.993 --> 00:11:37.790
- Is there anybody on the panel lost a job

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:42.570
or significant piece of income
because of the pandemic?

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:46.050
- So I own a private
practice optometric practice,

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:48.220
and so we were forced to close.

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:51.760
So I ended up having to
lay off my entire staff.

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:52.958
- Are you open again?

00:11:52.958 --> 00:11:54.300
- Yeah.

00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:55.860
- Give me your sense

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:57.910
for how you think president Trump

00:11:57.910 --> 00:11:59.750
has handled this situation.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:02.230
- I think he's done a good job

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:06.270
as far as letting the states
determine each individual state

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:08.213
on how they wanna handle it because

00:12:08.213 --> 00:12:11.984
when New York was being so
burdened, Wisconsin had nothing.

00:12:11.984 --> 00:12:15.110
- We can't blame Trump
for the virus of course.

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:16.660
And I don't even really blame him

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:19.110
for his initial actions or inactions

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:22.680
but I think now, especially
six months plus later,

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:24.890
they are holding and having these rallies,

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.970
political rallies with hundreds of people,

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:30.730
or sometimes even thousands in
a closed space without masks

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:33.990
and him continuing to attack people

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:37.380
or make fun of people who wear
masks including Joe Biden.

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:41.690
I think to me that is probably
what bothers me the most.

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:43.480
- And we should not have this many people

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:45.580
in the United States who died from this.

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:47.560
So the response was not quick enough.

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:50.596
It was not to the degree
that it should have been.

00:12:50.596 --> 00:12:53.370
And they had disproportionate outcomes

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:54.400
for different communities.

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:56.800
There's more black folks
who have died from this.

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:59.318
There are more Latinos
who are dying from this.

00:12:59.318 --> 00:13:01.740
This is not fair.

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:03.620
- How about your local
and state officials?

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:06.420
Do you feel like they've done a better

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:09.230
or worse job than
Washington on this issue?

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:11.990
- It's very inconsistent
which creates confusion.

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:14.820
We literally have school
districts within Ozaki County

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:16.170
that have different policies

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:19.110
about how they're handling
kids going back to school.

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:21.800
What makes Port Washington
different from Macon?

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:26.010
- You have the liberal areas
saying science shut down,

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:28.420
forget the economy, everyone's dying.

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:32.260
Conservative areas are saying open it up,

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:34.820
we got to have an economy freedom

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:37.390
and those neighborhoods are
very close to each other.

00:13:37.390 --> 00:13:40.040
So it's kind of like within
five minutes you can be

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:43.000
in three different zones of opinion.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:46.090
I generally follow the policy
of what my client wants.

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:49.240
So when my client shows up
in a mask, I put on a mask.

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:51.970
If my client asks me to
take it off, I take it off.

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.910
- Everybody has since agreed

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:55.660
everything has been politicized.

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:58.120
When I see clients, I wear a mask,

00:13:58.120 --> 00:14:00.490
My clients wear a mask in my office.

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:02.340
I have a hand sanitizer,

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:06.010
not because I'm afraid, I'd
rather be in on the safe side,

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:07.070
why take a chance?

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:11.240
Why would I wanna be responsible
of infecting somebody

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:14.500
and that person potentially
could die because

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:17.463
of how I do things?

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:21.630
I definitely don't want
the economy shut down,

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:23.850
I wanna see customers, I
wanna take care of them.

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:26.710
I'll see them in my
office anytime, any day,

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:28.990
but with the proper precaution.

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:33.433
- The economy and the pandemic
are very much intertwined.

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:38.100
Chris talk a little bit about
your real estate business

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:40.070
and what you've seen.

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:42.990
- When the pandemic
started I was very nervous

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:44.810
and braced for the worst.

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:45.960
The real estate economy which

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:47.605
to me has always been an indicator,

00:14:47.605 --> 00:14:50.930
obviously for me personally
it's my business,

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:52.830
has been amazing.

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:53.663
- Raise your hand

00:14:53.663 --> 00:14:56.020
if you thought the economy was pretty good

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:57.283
in January and February.

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:01.840
Everybody else has their
hands up other than Sabrina,

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:04.080
she's still kind of not sure

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.510
that the economy was that great.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:08.480
Now raise your hand
again if you're satisfied

00:15:08.480 --> 00:15:10.653
with the economy as it is today.

00:15:12.093 --> 00:15:14.580
- I think so many people I feel look

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.580
at the stock market as the economy

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:18.400
or what you're seeing your 401k,

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:19.470
but when you look at Milwaukee,

00:15:19.470 --> 00:15:22.860
it's kind of like inequities
the average suburban

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:24.410
or those of us in these counties,

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:26.820
maybe our economy or whatever is fine,

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:30.020
but when you look at the city
of Milwaukee in certain areas,

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:31.720
I don't think our economy is fine.

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:35.160
- Bernie you work with
a lot of immigrants.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:37.197
What's your take on sort of
how new immigrants are doing

00:15:37.197 --> 00:15:39.140
in the economy right now?

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:41.100
- Definitely not doing very well

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:43.010
because well number one,

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:46.250
a lot of the immigrants didn't qualify

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:49.010
for these stimulus checks.

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:50.350
So overall a lot

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:55.150
of the huge Latino community
is impacted negativity.

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:56.580
- Sue what is your sense

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:59.660
as a business owner just
for the economy sort

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:01.560
of writ large in your area?

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:03.090
- The economy, yes Is coming back.

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:05.680
Is it back 100% in certain fields?

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:06.513
I believe it is,

00:16:06.513 --> 00:16:10.440
but certain fields it is
nowhere near a hundred percent.

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.630
You start having people lose their jobs

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:14.633
then they lose their insurance.

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:17.890
It's all a chain reaction
or a trickle down effect.

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:20.050
If we don't save our economy,

00:16:20.050 --> 00:16:22.240
it's gonna affect many many more lives

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:24.040
than this pandemic will.

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:27.710
So I do believe that we
need to be very protective

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:30.620
of our economy and get things moving.

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:35.340
Yes, do it safely, but
we cannot just keep,

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:39.130
we can't all lock ourselves
in and shut everything down.

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:42.360
It's just going to be a disaster

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:46.290
- We've gleaned tonight that
there's there's division here

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:49.370
in the suburbs of Milwaukee,

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:53.900
differing opinions not unlike
the rest of the country.

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:55.130
Some of you have who have lived

00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:57.500
in the area for longer times.

00:16:57.500 --> 00:17:00.940
Can you just talk about
how the area is changing

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:05.670
and sort of if you sense
more political division

00:17:07.967 --> 00:17:10.840
as the area has diversified?

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:13.430
- This community was
always very Republican

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:18.360
and now there's Biden signs out there.

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:23.333
I think it's very divided
within neighborhoods,

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:26.700
which we've never seen before.

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:29.565
- Other than when I was serving
in different duty stations

00:17:29.565 --> 00:17:33.850
I've always came back to Waukesha
and I've been through 89.

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:37.470
At that time, there was a
very few Latino families.

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:39.700
It's grown tremendously over the years.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:42.980
Traditionally, the
Latinos vote more Democrat

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:45.780
- Being aware of the history
of Wisconsin and the red lining

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:48.530
that caused these suburbs to stay so white

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:51.160
and how those barriers
are starting to be removed

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:54.220
and allowing people to move
out into areas really allows

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:56.142
for a diversity to exist.

00:17:56.142 --> 00:17:59.230
And I do appreciate the fact
that there's different voices

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:01.650
to speak to different
people who are available.

00:18:01.650 --> 00:18:04.550
I do like different ideas.

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:06.010
- The question isn't necessarily

00:18:06.010 --> 00:18:08.360
whether Trump will win

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:11.540
these suburban Milwaukee
counties probably will,

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:14.430
but it'll depend on how much
margin he gets and then how

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:18.320
that affects the overall statewide
totals here in Wisconsin.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:20.510
What do you guys think?

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:22.890
- I feel a lot of
leadership pushing people

00:18:22.890 --> 00:18:25.130
to register and to vote and

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:29.750
if we get everybody coming out
and we increase the voting,

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:34.750
we already got a Democrat
governor last time.

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:38.391
So we actually I think that is going blue

00:18:38.391 --> 00:18:39.880
and I see that trend.

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:41.970
So as long as people get out and vote,

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:45.150
I think that Trump will lose in the state.

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:47.010
- Chris what's gonna happen in Wisconsin?

00:18:47.010 --> 00:18:49.590
- I think Trump will do
very well in Waukesha County

00:18:49.590 --> 00:18:50.610
and Washington County,

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:54.017
Ozaki County is the one
that is I think the closest.

00:18:54.017 --> 00:18:58.080
The question will there
be enough votes rural

00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:00.900
in rural Wisconsin to
offset the huge turnout

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:03.640
in Madison and Milwaukee
and that's usually the game.

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:06.740
I think Trump will win
and I'm counting on it.

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:10.005
I'm nervous, but I'm hopeful.

00:19:10.005 --> 00:19:12.422
(soft music)

